  "_comment": "Animals are skinned models from res://models/animals.glb (ITHappy 'Animals FREE' pack, free for commercial use). 'body_bones' are the torso segments the LONG/SHORT trait pushes apart - translating bones rather than scaling them is what stretches the torso without stretching the head, legs or tail. 'legs' lists each leg's telescoping segments in the order they pop out for TALL. 'stand_height' is the display height every animal is normalised to. Socket offsets are in those normalised units, Y up. 'bulk' groups the bones STRONG/WEAK thickens; 'inherits' names the group a group is nested inside so its scale can be divided out and the five controls stay independent. 'veins' are cartoon vein clusters that pop in on the biggest muscles. 'flourish' picks the species finishing pose.",
